+    # 200, same JSON as the 201 body (including `householdId`, `null` for plans without a household)
+
+### Households
+
+A household groups plans. Households cannot be deleted or renamed. Like every write, `POST /households` is unauthenticated (see the security note above), and any caller can attach a plan to any household.
+
+#### POST /households
+
+    curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/households -d '{"name":"Smith family"}'
+    # 201 {"id":"7b1e...","name":"Smith family"}
+
+`name` is required: a string whose trimmed length is 1 to 200 (stored trimmed), otherwise `400 name: required, non-empty string up to 200 characters`. A body that is not a JSON object gives `400 body: must be a JSON object`. Each call creates a new household; duplicate names are allowed.
+
+#### GET /households/:id
+
+    # 200 {"id":"7b1e...","name":"Smith family"}; unknown id: 404 {"error":"household not found"}
+
+#### GET /households/:id/plans
+
+    # 200 [{"id":"3f0c...","weekStart":"2025-01-06"}], ordered by weekStart then id; [] when empty; unknown household: 404
+
+#### `householdId` on POST /plans
+
+`householdId` is optional in the `POST /plans` body. Absent or `null` means no household. A non-string gives `400 householdId: must be a string`; a string that matches no household (including `""`) gives `404 household not found`. All body validation (400) happens first, then the household check (404), and only then Mealie is called. The plan response (POST and GET) always contains `householdId` (string or `null`).

