--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -14,6 +14,36 @@ npm test

 The server listens on all interfaces at `PORT`. SIGINT and SIGTERM close the server and the database. Logs go to stderr. If the database cannot be opened or a migration fails, the process exits with code 1.

+## API
+
+All responses are JSON; every error is `{"error":"<message>"}`. Unknown route 404, wrong method 405, body over 102400 bytes 413, Mealie failure or unset `MEALIE_URL` 502, unexpected error 500.
+
+| Route | Success | Errors |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /health` | 200 `{"ok":true}` | |
+| `POST /plans` | 201 plan | 400 invalid input, 409 no eligible recipe, 413, 502 |
+| `GET /plans/:id` | 200 plan | 404 `plan not found` |
+| `GET /plans/:id/shopping-list[?groupBy=label]` | 200 list | 400 bad `groupBy`, 404, 502 |
+
+`POST /plans` body: `{"weekStart":"YYYY-MM-DD" (a Monday), "days":1..14, "rules":{"mealsPerDay":1..3, "includeTags":[], "excludeTags":[], "maxTotalTimeMinutes":null, "diet":[]}}`.
+
+### Diet filters
+
+`rules.diet` is an optional array of `"vegetarian"`, `"vegan"` and `"gluten-free"` (exact, case-sensitive; anything else is 400). Food labels come from Mealie `GET /api/foods`. A recipe is excluded when any ingredient's food carries a banned label (exact label name): vegetarian bans `Meat` and `Fish`; vegan bans `Meat`, `Fish`, `Dairy` and `Egg`; gluten-free bans `Gluten`. Food names match case-insensitively; a food not in the list has no label. Diets combine (union of banned labels) and also combine with the tag and time rules. If no recipe is left the answer is 409. Without `diet`, `/api/foods` is not called.
+
+```
+curl -X POST localhost:3000/plans -H 'content-type: application/json' \
+  -d '{"weekStart":"2024-03-04","days":7,"rules":{"diet":["vegan","gluten-free"]}}'
+```
+
+### Shopping list grouped by label
+
+`GET /plans/:id/shopping-list` returns `{"planId","items":[{"food","quantity","unit"}],"notes":[]}`. With `?groupBy=label` it returns `{"planId","groups":[{"label","items":[...]}],"notes":[]}`: the same items, each in the group of its food's label (`Other` when there is none), groups sorted by label with `Other` last. Any other `groupBy` value (including empty) is 400 `groupBy must be "label"`.
+
+```
+curl 'localhost:3000/plans/<id>/shopping-list?groupBy=label'
+```
+
 ## Environment variables

 | Variable | Default | Meaning |
